  "response_text": "Once we had MSP_INIT_VAL, which tells where the main stack starts in memory, we calculated a new PSP_val by subtracting 0x400 from it. This gave a new memory location below the main stack that could be used as the starting point for the process stack. We needed the initial MSP location so we could allocate a new stack region without overlapping the main one. It also allows us to treat the stack space as a large block of memory to be divided into different chunks.\\n",
